  "development_selection_note": "Exploratory schedule selected after representation inspection. Layer 57 / decision and indices 50 through 69 reuse development data. All four cells and all selected kinds are assigned independently of source correctness or format validity. The original whole-instrument gate remains failed; the bound certificate authorizes this development scope only.",
  "planned_contrasts_note": "Direct within-prefix arm differences, complete four-cell worlds before gain stratification, and whole-world bootstrap sampling. Families and kinds remain separate; no pooled family endpoint. Bonferroni adjustment covers the 112 specified family/kind/revision endpoints only and does not account for prior site selection, development reuse, or other exploratory analyses. Percentile intervals are approximate and conditional on frozen fitted directions; they do not establish confirmatory error control. No p-values or inner-experience inference. Memory and instrument margins have their own meanings and are not pooled with information-judgment margins.",
  "dose_note": "Every direction is normalized at runtime. All nonzero doses use the pooled:balanced information contrast norm at layer 57 / decision, including answer, known, query, and seeded-random controls. Positive semantic information margin means Yes for new and No for repeat; positive memory margin means stronger correct-answer preference, and positive instrument margin means report versus stop."
